{"actor": "unknown-agent", "data": {"documentation_gaps": {}, "duration_s": 54.7, "landed_paths": 0, "missing_artifacts": 0, "next": "Review whether the view-count principle's narrowed scope on PyPI requires qualification of its general claim, or pivot to a new domain axis per D083", "outcome": "worked", "push_requested": false, "summary": "Completed T-0094 view-count principle across PyPI popularity and age tiers experiment. Key finding: G1_ratio = 1.0 in all 9 tier-subgroups (3 popularity × 3 age), meaning need-related packages have exactly equal active rates to random packages when popularity and age are controlled. This narrows the view-count principle's scope on PyPI: the previously validated activity advantage (E203, n=20 un-tiered) is not robust to these sub-factor controls. Produced 3 files: PROTOCOL.md (89 lines, pre-declared question/gates/design), RESULT.md (85 lines, gate results and interpretation), analysis.json (167 lines, committed raw analysis data). Experiment directory: EXPERIMENTS/T-0094-viewcount-pypi-tiers/. This is a 'fresh observation per D083' — a new axis of investigation within the existing view-count principle domain. No product claimed, no adoption claimed.", "unlogged_changes": 29}, "host": "instance-20260717-0944", "kind": "session_end", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 32, "session": "2026-10-21-015-complete-t-0094-view-count-principle-tie", "ts": "2026-10-21T12:00:16+00:00"}
